# Cache-Control is declared once, on /*. Two matching blocks do not override,
# they join: repeating this line under /src/* served every module a doubled
# max-age, which a cache is free to treat as stale. /src/* inherits it and adds
# only CORS.
#
# No stale-while-revalidate: clay.js imports ~49 unversioned module URLs, each
# with its own freshness clock, and a view-mode load fetches a different subset
# than an edit-mode load. A stale window lets one browser hold half the graph
# from before a deploy and half from after, which fails silently.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600

/src/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
